 "title": "Notion says a breach at its AI supplier Fireworks AI exposed Notion AI chat transcripts (inputs and replies, from data used for the Insights admin feature) from fewer than 1% of Notion workspaces; most cannot be tied to a user or workspace; Notion cut Fireworks off and deleted the data there on 3 Nov 2026, disabled Insights, says Fireworks kept data despite a zero-retention commitment; Fireworks says attackers came in through a third-party cloud provider (its second breach in about two months per TechCrunch/BleepingComputer); Notion's 9 Nov advisory: affected workspaces should rotate any passwords/API keys pasted into Notion AI, check via desktop Help (?) > Security incident review; no notice means no action for now",
